  "lectures": [
    {
      "id": "6656224",
      "title": "Injecting Services into Services",
      "lectureOrder": 436,
      "videoOrder": 400,
      "sourceHash": "1eeab4c1be4af0fb16a2b2eacdd0ecd27475e0e602fb7a771ce4910ebac60a74",
      "cues": [
        {
          "id": 1,
          "start": 3.15,
          "end": 3.983,
          "en": "-: In the last lecture,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 2,
          "start": 3.983,
          "end": 6.66,
          "en": "we learned about this hierarchical injector,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 3,
          "start": 6.66,
          "end": 10.14,
          "en": "and that we can choose between one instance",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 4,
          "start": 10.14,
          "end": 13.65,
          "en": "or multiple instances of the same service class.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 5,
          "start": 13.65,
          "end": 16.68,
          "en": "I mentioned that the highest possible level",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 6,
          "start": 16.68,
          "end": 18.84,
          "en": "is actually not the AppComponent.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 7,
          "start": 18.84,
          "end": 21.15,
          "en": "So let's remove it here, this providers array,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 8,
          "start": 21.15,
          "end": 24.33,
          "en": "leave it in the the constructor and leave the import,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 9,
          "start": 24.33,
          "end": 28.02,
          "en": "but the highest possible level is in the AppModule.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 10,
          "start": 28.02,
          "end": 30.96,
          "en": "Here, we also have a providers array added",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 11,
          "start": 30.96,
          "end": 32.58,
          "en": "if you don't have it,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 12,
          "start": 32.58,
          "end": 36.66,
          "en": "and here we can also provide the AccountsService.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 13,
          "start": 36.66,
          "end": 40.083,
          "en": "Make sure to also add the import at the top here, then.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 14,
          "start": 41.37,
          "end": 43.44,
          "en": "With that little addition here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 15,
          "start": 43.44,
          "end": 46.44,
          "en": "we're making sure that our whole application,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 16,
          "start": 46.44,
          "end": 50.19,
          "en": "everything in our application receives the same instance",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 17,
          "start": 50.19,
          "end": 53.193,
          "en": "of the service unless it overrides it as we did before.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 18,
          "start": 54.12,
          "end": 57.63,
          "en": "Now with that, we can now even inject a service",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 19,
          "start": 57.63,
          "end": 59.7,
          "en": "into a number of service,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 20,
          "start": 59.7,
          "end": 61.71,
          "en": "because that's not possible by providing it",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 21,
          "start": 61.71,
          "end": 62.85,
          "en": "on a component level,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 22,
          "start": 62.85,
          "end": 66.6,
          "en": "for that we need to provide it in the AppModule.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 23,
          "start": 66.6,
          "end": 69.45,
          "en": "So, let's say we want to log something,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 24,
          "start": 69.45,
          "end": 73.38,
          "en": "if we call action in the AccountsService.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 25,
          "start": 73.38,
          "end": 76.41,
          "en": "So I would have to provide a LoggingService",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 26,
          "start": 76.41,
          "end": 78.66,
          "en": "in my AppModule now,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 27,
          "start": 78.66,
          "end": 82.32,
          "en": "and therefore I will simply comment out providers here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 28,
          "start": 82.32,
          "end": 85.32300000000001,
          "en": "in my @Component decorators.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 29,
          "start": 86.28,
          "end": 90.66,
          "en": "And I don't want to call LoggingService here anymore,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 30,
          "start": 90.66,
          "end": 92.94,
          "en": "so we'll comment this out",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 31,
          "start": 92.94,
          "end": 95.28,
          "en": "and I will actually leave the injection here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 32,
          "start": 95.28,
          "end": 98.03999999999999,
          "en": "so that you have it for reference if you download the code.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 33,
          "start": 98.03999999999999,
          "end": 101.52000000000001,
          "en": "I'll also comment it out here in new account component.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 34,
          "start": 101.52000000000001,
          "end": 104.328,
          "en": "Instead, let's say I want to use this LoggingService",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 35,
          "start": 104.328,
          "end": 105.63,
          "en": "in the AccountsService,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 36,
          "start": 105.63,
          "end": 109.2,
          "en": "and I might want to call the log status change method there",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 37,
          "start": 109.2,
          "end": 112.17,
          "en": "because this isn't the enter place where the status changes,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 38,
          "start": 112.17,
          "end": 113.88,
          "en": "either because we added a new account",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 39,
          "start": 113.88,
          "end": 116.253,
          "en": "or because we called update status.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 40,
          "start": 117.12,
          "end": 119.88,
          "en": "So to use the service there,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 41,
          "start": 119.88,
          "end": 121.59,
          "en": "generally we start in the same way.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 42,
          "start": 121.59,
          "end": 125.6,
          "en": "We add a constructor and we inject our LoggingService.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 43,
          "start": 125.6,
          "end": 130.6,
          "en": "In this case, set the type, import this type at the top,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 44,
          "start": 130.68,
          "end": 133.14,
          "en": "make sure to add the import.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 45,
          "start": 133.14,
          "end": 135.48,
          "en": "And we provided it an AppModule.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 46,
          "start": 135.48,
          "end": 137.61,
          "en": "So you could think that we are set to go,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 47,
          "start": 137.61,
          "end": 141.63,
          "en": "that we can now go to add account, call LoggingService,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 48,
          "start": 141.63,
          "end": 145.56,
          "en": "log the status change, pass the status here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 49,
          "start": 145.56,
          "end": 148.2,
          "en": "and do the same here for updates status.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 50,
          "start": 148.2,
          "end": 150.18,
          "en": "You could think this is how we do it",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 51,
          "start": 150.18,
          "end": 152.43,
          "en": "and it's not unlogical to think so,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 52,
          "start": 152.43,
          "end": 154.98,
          "en": "but let's see if this works.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 53,
          "start": 154.98,
          "end": 158.977,
          "en": "If we load our app, we already get an error.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 54,
          "start": 158.977,
          "end": 162.75,
          "en": "\"Can't resolve all parameters for AccountsService.\"",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 55,
          "start": 162.75,
          "end": 164.313,
          "en": "Something's not working.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 56,
          "start": 165.32999999999998,
          "end": 169.26,
          "en": "The reason is, if you inject a service into something,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 57,
          "start": 169.26,
          "end": 174.06,
          "en": "this something needs to have some metadata attached to it.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 58,
          "start": 174.06,
          "end": 175.95,
          "en": "Now, a component has some metadata",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 59,
          "start": 175.95,
          "end": 177.78300000000002,
          "en": "because we have @Component.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 60,
          "start": 178.82999999999998,
          "end": 182.58,
          "en": "A directive has some metadata because we have @Directive.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 61,
          "start": 182.58,
          "end": 187.41,
          "en": "Account or, excuse me, a service doesn't have any metadata.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 62,
          "start": 187.41,
          "end": 188.7,
          "en": "It's just how Angular works",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 63,
          "start": 188.7,
          "end": 190.38,
          "en": "that we need to attach some metadata,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 64,
          "start": 190.38,
          "end": 192.24,
          "en": "and of course, not any metadata.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 65,
          "start": 192.24,
          "end": 195.03,
          "en": "You shouldn't attach @Component here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 66,
          "start": 195.03,
          "end": 196.56,
          "en": "There is a specific metadata",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 67,
          "start": 196.56,
          "end": 198.57,
          "en": "you should attach in such cases.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 68,
          "start": 198.57,
          "end": 202.53,
          "en": "It's @Injectable, which needs to be imported",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 69,
          "start": 202.53,
          "end": 204.87,
          "en": "from @angularcore.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 70,
          "start": 204.87,
          "end": 209.87,
          "en": "This tells Angular that now this service is is injectable",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 71,
          "start": 209.88,
          "end": 213.27,
          "en": "or that something can be injected in there, to be precise.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 72,
          "start": 213.27,
          "end": 214.82999999999998,
          "en": "So that's important.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 73,
          "start": 214.82999999999998,
          "end": 219.39,
          "en": "You don't add @Injectable to the service you want to inject,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 74,
          "start": 219.39,
          "end": 222.6,
          "en": "but to the service where you want to inject something.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 75,
          "start": 222.6,
          "end": 224.91,
          "en": "So the receiving service you could say,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 76,
          "start": 224.91,
          "end": 227.67000000000002,
          "en": "that to be injected in service.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 77,
          "start": 227.67000000000002,
          "end": 230.25,
          "en": "And you don't need to add it to any other service.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 78,
          "start": 230.25,
          "end": 232.68,
          "en": "If you don't want to inject anything in a service,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 79,
          "start": 232.68,
          "end": 234.42000000000002,
          "en": "like here for the LoggingService,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 80,
          "start": 234.42000000000002,
          "end": 236.64,
          "en": "you don't need to add @Injectable.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 81,
          "start": 236.64,
          "end": 241.5,
          "en": "Only add it if you expect to get something injected.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 82,
          "start": 241.5,
          "end": 243.3,
          "en": "Now, one important note here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 83,
          "start": 243.3,
          "end": 246.24,
          "en": "as I explained, we don't need to add injectable,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 84,
          "start": 246.24,
          "end": 249.06,
          "en": "the injectable decorator here to this class,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 85,
          "start": 249.06,
          "end": 250.44,
          "en": "because this is a service",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 86,
          "start": 250.44,
          "end": 252.81,
          "en": "which we only inject somewhere else,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 87,
          "start": 252.81,
          "end": 256.05,
          "en": "but where we don't inject anything into this service.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 88,
          "start": 256.05,
          "end": 258.45,
          "en": "And you technically really only need injectable",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 89,
          "start": 258.45,
          "end": 260.61,
          "en": "if you inject something into this service,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 90,
          "start": 260.61,
          "end": 264.48,
          "en": "not if you just inject this service somewhere else.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 91,
          "start": 264.48,
          "end": 268.32,
          "en": "In newer versions of Angler, however, it is recommended",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 92,
          "start": 268.32,
          "end": 270.96,
          "en": "that you always add @Injectable.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 93,
          "start": 270.96,
          "end": 273.18,
          "en": "It technically makes no difference right now,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 94,
          "start": 273.18,
          "end": 274.89,
          "en": "in the future it might though,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 95,
          "start": 274.89,
          "end": 278.25,
          "en": "so it's already a habit you might get into that you add it.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 96,
          "start": 278.25,
          "end": 281.82,
          "en": "Here, I do omit it, but you could consider adding it also,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 97,
          "start": 281.82,
          "end": 285.36,
          "en": "to ensure that in the future, it doesn't unexpectedly break.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 98,
          "start": 285.36,
          "end": 287.31,
          "en": "What I explained about why you need it",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 99,
          "start": 287.31,
          "end": 289.08,
          "en": "and that you don't need it here technically,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 100,
          "start": 289.08,
          "end": 290.97,
          "en": "still holds though.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 101,
          "start": 290.97,
          "end": 294.81,
          "en": "With this, if I now save this and we let the app reload,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 102,
          "start": 294.81,
          "end": 298.77,
          "en": "now it works, and now you see that if I save this,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 103,
          "start": 298.77,
          "end": 302.07,
          "en": "we still log it to the console with the correct status.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 104,
          "start": 302.07,
          "end": 304.02,
          "en": "The same happens if I click here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 105,
          "start": 304.02,
          "end": 307.2,
          "en": "but now everything is centralized into our service,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 106,
          "start": 307.2,
          "end": 310.743,
          "en": "and now we're also injecting a service into a service.",
          "zh": ""
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
  "errors": []
}
